# UST.G3FX Component-20 Adjugate Normal-Homotopy Theorem

## Result

Let

```text
q=xz-y^2,  r=w+G3,  rbar=w-G3,
K3=q H4+r rbar,
```

and form the normal Jacobian

```text
J = d(q,H4,rbar,r)/d(x,y,z,w).
```

The frozen q79 residue theorem gives

```text
det J = 6 P_delta.
```

For the exact selected normal source from G3FI,

```text
R=q D7+r B6,
```

define

```text
v=(0,D7,B6,0)^T,
h=adj(J) v.
```

Then, coefficientwise in all six power-basis coordinates of `Q(gamma)`,

```text
h dot grad(K3) = 6 P_delta R.
```

This is a literal polynomial identity. No division by `rbar`, `P_delta` or
any fitted scalar is used.

## Why this is the missing kind of map

The first three entries of `h` have weighted degree 10 and the fourth has
weighted degree 12. These are exactly the frozen coefficient degrees of the
Macaulay columns generated by

```text
dPhi/dx, dPhi/dy, dPhi/dz, dPhi/dw.
```

These are the correct *bare* base degrees for a Jacobian homotopy. Full Cox
bookkeeping adds the component multiplier and exposes an important boundary.
The frozen H02 target has degree `(9,1,2)`, whereas the adjugate identity lands
in `(15,1,2)`. The difference is exactly

```text
deg P_delta=(6,0,0).
```

Thus `h` is the explicit integral numerator of a localized homotopy. It is
not yet a same-degree compiler into the G3EX presentation.

## First nonlinear repair

For

```text
Phi=u K3+v E+s F_selected,
```

the identity becomes

```text
s h dot grad_X(Phi)
 = 6 P_delta u s R + s^2 h dot grad_X(F_selected).
```

The first term cancels the `P_delta`-multiplied normal source in the higher
Cox degree. The second is not discarded: it is the explicit next
homological-repair defect. This gives a rigorous numerator for the
homological-perturbation series anticipated by G3FH--G3FK.

## Boundary

G3FX does not prove that `P_delta` is invertible or saturated on the selected
quotient, that residue duality removes the six-degree shift, that the `s^2`
defect vanishes, or that the full repair terminates. It does not yet emit the
100 G3EX zero-residual relations or prove component rank 36.

The next calculation is now two-stage. First prove `P_delta` saturation on
the selected 100-plane, or construct the exact residue-duality descent from
degree `(15,1,2)` to `(9,1,2)`. Only after that descent is legal should one
compute

```text
R1=h dot grad_X(F_selected),
```

and reduce it through the regular normal pair and the integral
`Sym^15/q^4 Sym^7` normal form, and iterate only if the resulting defect stays
in the selected finite Cox degree.

